{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Symbol","language":"Translingual","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt7\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span><span about=\"#mwt7\"> </span><i about=\"#mwt7\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO%20639-3\" title=\"w:ISO 639-3\" class=\"extiw\">ISO 639-3</a><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:ISO_639-3\"> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/language_code\" title=\"language code\">language code</a> for </i><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO%20639:and\" title=\"w:ISO 639:and\" about=\"#mwt7\" class=\"extiw\"><b>Ansus</b></a><i about=\"#mwt7\">.</i>"}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Conjunction","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\n<ol><li>Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. <style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r90144991\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt84\">.mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}</style>\n</li>\n<li>Simply connecting two clauses or sentences. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt93\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">\n</li>\n<li>Introducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt97\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<i>I'd been walking since sunrise, <b>and</b> I was hungry.</i>"},{"example":"<i>Two <b>and</b> two is/are four</i>."}],"examples":["<i>I'd been walking since sunrise, <b>and</b> I was hungry.</i>","<i>Two <b>and</b> two is/are four</i>."]},{"definition":"Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. <style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r90144991\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt84\">.mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}</style>"},{"definition":"Simply connecting two clauses or sentences. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt93\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"Introducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt97\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<i>I'd been walking since sunrise, <b>and</b> I was hungry.</i>"}],"examples":["<i>I'd been walking since sunrise, <b>and</b> I was hungry.</i>"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt101\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/yet\" title=\"yet\">Yet</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/but\" title=\"but\">but</a>. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt102\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"Used to connect certain numbers: connecting units when they precede tens ; connecting shillings to pence in a monetary quantity ; connecting tens and units to hundreds, thousands etc. (now often omitted in US); to connect fractions to wholes. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt107\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt113\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Used to connect more than two elements together in a chain, sometimes to stress the number of elements."},{"definition":"Connecting two identical elements, with implications of continued or infinite repetition. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt115\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"Introducing a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/parenthetical\" title=\"parenthetical\">parenthetical</a> or explanatory clause. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt119\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"Introducing the continuation of narration from a previous understood point; also used alone as a question: ‘and so what?’."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt126\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Used to connect two verbs where the second is dependent on the first: ‘<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/to\" title=\"to\">to</a>’. Used especially after <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt127\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/come#English\" title=\"come\">come</a></i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt128\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/go#English\" title=\"go\">go</a></i> and <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt129\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/try#English\" title=\"try\">try</a></i>. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt130\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"Introducing a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/qualitative\" title=\"qualitative\">qualitative</a> difference between things having the same name; “as well as other”. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt135\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"Used to combine numbers in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/addition\" title=\"addition\">addition</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/plus\" title=\"plus\">plus</a> (with singular or plural verb). <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt139\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<i>Two <b>and</b> two is/are four</i>."}],"examples":["<i>Two <b>and</b> two is/are four</i>."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt143\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <i>Expressing a condition.</i>\n<ol><li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt144\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/if\" title=\"if\">If</a>; provided that. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt145\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">\n</li>\n<li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt150\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/as_if\" title=\"as if\">As if</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/as_though\" title=\"as though\">as though</a>. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt151\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">\n</li></ol>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt144\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/if\" title=\"if\">If</a>; provided that. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt145\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt150\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/as_if\" title=\"as if\">As if</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/as_though\" title=\"as though\">as though</a>. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt151\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt155\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Connecting two <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/well-formed_formula\" title=\"well-formed formula\">well-formed formulas</a> to create a new well-formed formula that requires it to only be true when both of the two formulas are true."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":""},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\"></span> In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/rhythm\" title=\"rhythm\">rhythm</a>, the second half of a divided <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/beat\" title=\"beat\">beat</a>."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt195\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/breath\" title=\"breath\">Breath</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt196\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea%20smoke\" title=\"w:Sea smoke\" about=\"#mwt197\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" class=\"extiw\">Sea smoke</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/steam_fog\" title=\"steam fog\">steam fog</a>."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Verb","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt212\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/breathe\" title=\"breathe\">breathe</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/whisper\" title=\"whisper\">whisper</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/devise\" title=\"devise\">devise</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/imagine\" title=\"imagine\">imagine</a>."}]}],"az":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"Azerbaijani","definitions":[{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/oath\" title=\"oath\">oath</a>"}]}],"da":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"Danish","definitions":[{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/duck\" title=\"duck\">duck</a> <spa